      <Desc>Over 400 recruiting organizations (mostly nonprofit colleges and universities) use the ECON JOB MARKET program to announce job openings and/or collect applications. ECON JOB MARKET Inc. promotes efficient exchange of job-market materials. THE ORGANIZATION HAS DEVELOPED A SET OF RELATED PROGRAMS IN FURTHERANCE OF THIS PURPOSE. THE MAIN PROGRAM IS ENTITLED, CENTRAL REPOSITORY FOR APPLICATION MATERIALS. THIS PROGRAM MAINTAINS A REPOSITORY FOR JOB-POSTINGS, APPLICATIONS, AND LETTERS OF RECOMMENDATION FOR THE ACADEMIC ECONOMICS JOB MARKET. OTHER PROGRAMS PROVIDE ANCILLARY SERVICES SUCH AS DATA TRANSFER TO RECRUITMENT SYSTEMS AND A PLATFORM FOR SCHEDULING INTERVIEWS. THE PROGRAMS ARE FUNDED MAINLY BY DONATIONS IN KIND, NAMELY HOURS OF SERVICE BY NUMEROUS VOLUNTEERS (INCLUDING DIRECTORS AND OFFICERS). ALSO, REVENUE IS GENERATED BY FEES THAT SOME OF THE RECRUITING ORGANIZATIONS AND CANDIDATES PAY.</Desc>
