        <ExplanationTxt>NO COMMITTEES OTHER THAN THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS EXIST</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE DIRECTORS REVIEW THE ORGANIZATION'S FINANCIALS WHEN SETTING THE YEARLY BUDGET DURING THE ANNUAL BOARD MEETING. SHORTLY THEREAFTER, FORM 990 IS PREPARED AND FILED. THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS ARE NOT ASKED TO REVIEW THE RETURN BEFORE FILING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The senior officers were allocated stipends for their extensive service to Econ Job Market in the fiscal year 2024-2025 (which ended 30 June 2025). The Disinterested Members of the Board of Directors determine the stipend amount each officer is to receive and certify that this compensation is appropriate by reviewing the officers time commitments and comparing their responsibilities with similar positions in the academic profession (such as journal editors). The Disinterested Members determined that the stipend amounts fall far short of fair and market compensation for their time, and hence the officers are partly volunteers. This determination is made no less than annually. Officers have the option of (a) receiving their stipends or (b) instructing the company to contribute the allocated funds to their university employers to support research activities, in lieu of stipend payments. Officer Martin Osborne elected to receive the stipend. The other officers elected to have their stipend funds contributed to their university employers.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
